// Buffers beyond rows a system appends: a fn reads one it is given
// (`bytes: Bytes`) and passes it on, also for each entity of a `for`; a
// proc changes one it is given `mut` (a row's field, a row more, none); a
// system changes a row (`Screen[i].pixel = ..`; nothing where there is no
// such row) and fills a buffer with rows alike (`Screen = [{ .. }; n]`);
// and a device is handed one to fill (Inputs/given/filled.ent, filled.c):
// where its count is, how many rows it holds, and its fields' values.
// RUN: %ent run -I %S/Inputs/given %S/Inputs/given.ent | FileCheck %s
// RUN: %ent run --parallel -I %S/Inputs/given %S/Inputs/given.ent | FileCheck %s
// RUN: %ent build -I %S/Inputs/given %S/Inputs/given.ent -o %t.exe --keep %t.dir
// RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HEADER --input-file=%t.dir/ent_extern.h

// HEADER-DAG: void ent_filled_fill_bytes(int32_t *arg0_count, int32_t arg0_capacity, uint8_t *arg0_value, int32_t arg1);
// HEADER-DAG: int32_t ent_filled_sum_bytes(int32_t arg0_count, const uint8_t *arg0_value);

// CHECK:      bytes 20: sum 1100 short 513 shorts 3081
// CHECK-NEXT: full 64
// CHECK-NEXT: screen 16: 1 44 -5 0
// CHECK-NEXT: line 66: 1 50 1 1
// CHECK-NEXT: more 17: 9 90
// CHECK-NEXT: dot at 1: 1
// CHECK-NEXT: dot at 12: 1
// CHECK-NEXT: total 27240
// CHECK-NEXT: none 0
// CHECK-NEXT: again 2: 3 0
// CHECK-NOT:  {{.}}
